WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.552
Start with the installation handover,

2
00:00:02.672 --> 00:00:05.253
configuration and finding register.

3
00:00:05.373 --> 00:00:07.787
Our earlier gasket-material gap has

4
00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:11.493
not disappeared merely because this is a
new module.

5
00:00:11.613 --> 00:00:14.165
For each proposed activity, establish

6
00:00:14.285 --> 00:00:17.595
whether it depends on that unresolved
component.

7
00:00:17.715 --> 00:00:20.957
Record a responsible decision before
execution;

8
00:00:21.077 --> 00:00:24.249
a high completion percentage is not
readiness.

9
00:00:24.869 --> 00:00:29.145
Identify the approved protocol, software
or parameter version,

10
00:00:29.265 --> 00:00:31.472
drawings and acceptance sources.

11
00:00:31.592 --> 00:00:34.045
The same test identifier run on two

12
00:00:34.165 --> 00:00:37.338
configurations may answer different
questions.

13
00:00:37.458 --> 00:00:39.719
Record changes and their impact.

14
00:00:39.839 --> 00:00:42.804
Supplier procedures can inform the
package,

15
00:00:42.924 --> 00:00:47.269
but the site must establish their
suitability for the installed

16
00:00:47.389 --> 00:00:49.608
system and intended activity.

17
00:00:50.228 --> 00:00:54.090
Plan trained personnel, suitable
calibrated instruments,

18
00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:56.919
access and engineering safety controls.

19
00:00:57.039 --> 00:01:00.074
This course does not teach bypassing
guards,

20
00:01:00.194 --> 00:01:04.539
isolating utilities or injecting faults
into working equipment.

21
00:01:04.659 --> 00:01:09.142
Such activities require approved methods
and competent personnel.

22
00:01:09.262 --> 00:01:13.193
A planned challenge must stay within the
equipment design

23
00:01:13.313 --> 00:01:15.318
and safe operating envelope.

24
00:01:15.938 --> 00:01:20.439
Annex 15 allows a documented conditional
next-stage decision

25
00:01:20.559 --> 00:01:25.594
where unresolved matters have no
significant impact on the next activity.

26
00:01:25.714 --> 00:01:27.714
In this fictional case,

27
00:01:27.834 --> 00:01:31.696
a separately assessed display review might
be considered

28
00:01:31.816 --> 00:01:34.299
while wetted challenges remain held.

29
00:01:34.419 --> 00:01:37.384
That example is a practical
recommendation,

30
00:01:37.504 --> 00:01:41.159
not automatic permission or prescribed
Annex wording.
